    "title": "Freedom of Expression Project prepares for upcoming exhibition showcasing local artists - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Samantha Mesa ,\n6 hours ago\nDES MOINES, Iowa — The Freedom of Expression (FOE) Project is just weeks aways from it’s THE WORLD WE BUILD exhibit which showcases local artists.\nLaunched in 2022, FOE is a biennial public arts and culture initiative that explores the intersections of human experience and the right to freedom of expression for individuals of all abilities using central Iowa artists across disciplines, abilities, and career stages to create collective exhibitions.\nAs both gallery exhibition and traveling show, THE WORLD WE BUILD offers audiences a sensory-rich experience of art that challenges convention, reimagines creative freedom, and insists on community at its core. You are invited to step into this space of process, connection, and radical self-expression.\nCurate Studio | Sept 16–19, 2025\nDes Moines Art Center, Education Wing | Sept 22–29, 2025\nPresented with support from:\nGreater Des Moines Public Art Foundation · Mosaic in Central Iowa · Des Moines Art\nCenter · Mainframe Studios · Nik Star Designs · The Healthy Project · Iowa Arts Council· Oakridge Neighborhood · PBS · Jill Wells Art · Iowa Department for the Blind · AXA Mentorship\nTo learn more visit the FOE Projects website.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to who13.com.",
